cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Threadfin: clone-level analysis of B-cell states from paired single-cell RNA-seq and BCR-seq"
message: "If you use Threadfin, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Satoshi
    given-names: Chen
    alias: Reynold4k
url: "https://github.com/Reynold4k/Threadfin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Reynold4k/Threadfin"
license: MIT
version: 4.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-02"
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - scRNA-seq
  - BCR
  - B cell
  - clonal lineage
  - germinal centre
  - immunology
abstract: >-
  Threadfin treats each B-cell clone as the unit of analysis in paired
  single-cell RNA-seq and BCR-seq data. It defines clones within donors,
  estimates shrunken, context-adjusted clone state profiles with explicit
  reliability, tests how much transcriptional variation is clonally
  inherited with sampling-aware permutation nulls, groups clones into
  bootstrap-stable clonal programmes, performs clone-level association tests
  and measures clonal memory across time points and tissues.
